# Boek de Bus — configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. Nothing here is required to run `bun dev`;
# every value has a development default. Two of them are required in production
# and the app refuses to start without them, which is deliberate.

# ── required in production ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Signs the session cookie. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Must be at least 32 characters. Outside production an insecure fixed default is
# used so that restarting the dev server does not sign you out; in production a
# missing or too-short value is a startup error, because a guessable value here
# means anyone can mint a session for anyone.
SESSION_SECRET=

# The app's own origin, used to build the links inside emails. Without it those
# links point at localhost.
APP_URL=https://boek-de-bus.example.com

# ── the household ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# There is no self-signup: these lists are the invitation. Only these addresses
# can request a sign-in link.
#
# Owners book outright and decide on other people's requests. Guests may only
# request. Names are derived from the address (jan@… becomes "Jan").
#
# These seed the in-memory stub repository. Once real Postgres is wired up (see
# src/lib/db/index.ts) they stop being used and the `users` table takes over.
OWNER_EMAILS=jan@example.com,els@example.com
GUEST_EMAILS=sanne@example.com,tom@example.com

# ── stubs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Email delivery is currently stubbed: messages are written to the server log
# instead of being sent, which means the sign-in link only exists in that log.
# Production refuses to boot in that state unless this is set, so that shipping
# without a mail provider has to be a decision rather than an oversight.
#
# Set to 1 only if you genuinely want a deployment where nobody can sign in
# without shell access to the logs.
# ALLOW_LOG_EMAIL=1

# When Postgres is added, its connection string goes here.
# DATABASE_URL=
